cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "rewardlint: adversarial auditing for RLVR reward functions"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: junglezke
repository-code: "https://github.com/junglezke/rewardlint"
abstract: >-
  rewardlint measures what an RLVR verifier accepts and rejects. It runs a
  reward function against a corpus of adversarial completions covering answer
  equivalence, genuine distinctions, realistic output formatting, and nine
  exploit strategies that a policy can reach by gradient descent without
  solving the task, and reports the resulting false-positive and false-negative
  rates together with the specific attacks that succeed.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - RLVR
  - reward hacking
  - verifier
  - large language models
  - evaluation
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
